<%- include('partials/legal-head') %>
      <p class="setup-eyebrow">Legal</p>
      <h1 class="setup-title">Cookie Policy</h1>
      <p class="setup-lead">
        Cookies and similar storage on Influzer.ai. This sits next to the <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.
      </p>
      <p class="legal-meta">Effective 24 October 2026 · <a href="/support">Contact</a></p>

      <section class="legal-block">
        <h2>1. What we store</h2>
        <div class="legal-table-wrap">
          <table class="legal-table">
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th>Name</th>
                <th>Purpose</th>
                <th>How long</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr>
                <td><code>connect.sid</code></td>
                <td>Keeps you signed in. Set only after you log in. HttpOnly.</td>
                <td>7 days</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td><code>_ga</code>, <code>_ga_*</code></td>
                <td>Google Analytics on pages that load our tag, including this one.</td>
                <td>Up to 2 years</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Google AdSense cookies</td>
                <td>Ads on the logo generator only.</td>
                <td>Set by Google</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td>Local storage</td>
                <td>Theme (light or dark) and, on the older tools, language. Not a cookie.</td>
                <td>Until you clear site data</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="legal-block">
        <h2>2. Why</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Essential.</strong> The session cookie is what keeps an account signed in.</li>
          <li><strong>Preferences.</strong> Theme and language stay on your device.</li>
          <li><strong>Analytics.</strong> Google Analytics tells us which pages are used.</li>
          <li><strong>Ads.</strong> The logo generator loads Google AdSense. The directory pages do not.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="legal-block">
        <h2>3. Third parties</h2>
        <p>
          Google Analytics and Google AdSense set their own cookies.
          Google or Facebook may set cookies if you use those sign-in buttons.
          Their policies govern those cookies. You can refuse non-essential cookies in your browser. Blocking <code>connect.sid</code> means you cannot stay signed in.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="legal-block">
        <h2>4. Do Not Track</h2>
        <p>Browsers can send a Do Not Track signal. There is no common rule for how sites must respond. We do not change our analytics based on that signal.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="legal-block">
        <h2>5. Changes</h2>
        <p>
          Updates are posted on this page. Questions: <a href="mailto:hello@influzer.ai">hello@influzer.ai</a> or the <a href="/support">support page</a>.
        </p>
      </section>
<%- include('partials/legal-foot') %>
